sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.157 µm on the D. yakuba abdominal cuticle (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 84.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg (a, b, D_u, D_v) = (0.10, 0.90, 1, 20) at geological age 0 Ma and scale 2.2 µm. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.995 against the discrete Laplacian. The equal-diffusion control has σ* = −0.102. The D_v sweep is monotone. The growth GIF is 12 frames at 640×480. The wavelength reported from 3×3 nearest neighbours is 1.332 µm (KS 0.592) because those neighbours sit along a spiral arm. That is not the arm-to-arm period. Predecessor D. willistoni remains at its cellular 86 µm band; the wavenumber ratio is 40.01. No successor (chronoseries 41/41). Overall 84.1/100 (faithfulness 82.4, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 1d40797a1aa1c46f0b61e38c4454905b1b892739; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_yakuba_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-yakuba-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 1d40797a1aa1c46f0b61e38c4454905b1b892739, image/png, 453541 B, 1248×960 px, artifact_sha256 5b349030a42551dc891b113c913f5633a1bdb089905cd189149489f0302eb3e2 (sha256 5b349030a42551dc891b113c913f5633a1bdb089905cd189149489f0302eb3e2), spec_fingerprint 92972fdde4bae9de4e9a6818d7f399847640e9a945f2f00a3077f1693c946f83. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 92972fdde4bae9de4e9a6818d7f399847640e9a945f2f00a3077f1693c946f83; artifact_sha256: 012a50ed1719b0b98fa95bbf04722cbf783e8f81f6c0fb6e8516a2e59886f126; input_dataset_sha256: {drosophila_yakuba_specimen.jpg=71ea43a85af08357...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952): diffusion-driven instability and a selected wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979): the a−u+u²v / b−u²v kinetics. | Carbone et al. (2005) and Llopart et al. (2002): the yakuba/santomea pigmentation difference is genetic. Wittkopp et al. (2002): Yellow and Ebony act reciprocally on melanin versus NBAD.; reconstructed_in_script: Linear dispersion (trace, determinant, cross term, discrete σ(q)) and an explicit-Euler Schnakenberg spiral on a 72×96 periodic patch, with λ* pinned to 2.157 µm. | Yellow = slow activator and Ebony/NBAD = fast substrate is an interpretive reading, not an equation in those papers.; transfer_boundary: A 16 µm periodic patch is not a whole tergite. The gallery specimen is a sepia gradation field, not a dissected cuticle micrograph at 2.2 µm.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Carbone et al. measured a 2.157 µm granule spacing, and does not copy the 97 µm cellular-tier yakuba sibling (slot 2731). | Pass 1 does not claim the 3×3 bead spacing equals λ*. That estimator is the remediation target.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Re-score morphometric-validation on the corrected wavelength against λ* = 2.157 µm, including the KS distance of the radial periods.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the 3×3 nearest-neighbour bead spacing (1.332 µm, KS 0.592) with the radial arm-to-arm period and the isotropic FFT ring, and keep the bead statistic only as a labelled diagnostic." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.841"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (Cursor cloud agent, primary assessor, pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

